        "id": "m6-theory",
        "title": "Diphthongs — Gliding Vowels",
        "type": "theory",
        "order": 1,
        "theoryHtml": "<h2>Diphthongs</h2><p>A diphthong starts at one vowel position and glides smoothly to another within a single syllable.</p><ul><li><strong>/eɪ/</strong> — <em>face, day</em>. Starts at /ɛ/, glides to /ɪ/.</li><li><strong>/aɪ/</strong> — <em>night, fire</em>. Starts at /a/, glides to /ɪ/.</li><li><strong>/ɔɪ/</strong> — <em>boy, coin</em>. Starts at /ɔ/, glides to /ɪ/.</li><li><strong>/aʊ/</strong> — <em>mouth, town</em>. Starts at /a/, glides to /ʊ/.</li><li><strong>/oʊ/</strong> — <em>note, home</em>. Starts at /o/, glides to /ʊ/.</li></ul><p>The glide must be smooth — both parts belong in one syllable.</p>",
        "words": []
